      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:5:11:4",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( عليه السلام ) إِنَّ شَهَادَةَ الصِّبْيَانِ إِذَا أَشْهَدُوهُمْ وَ هُمْ صِغَارٌ جَازَتْ إِذَا كَبِرُوا مَا لَمْ يَنْسَوْهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Al Nowfaly, from Al Sakuny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">asws</sup> having said: ‘Amir Al-Momineen<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">asws</sup> that the testimony of the children, when they are called as witnesses, and they are young, is allowed when they get older, what they have not forgotten’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Abu Ali al-Ash ‘ariy has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Jabbar from Safwan from al-‘Ala’ ibn Razin from Muhammad ibn Muslim who has narrated the following: “About the case of a child if his bearing testimony to an existing testimony, he (the Imam) said, ‘If his reason can comprehend when he becomes mature that it is right, it then is permissible.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
